<XMLBIBLE version="2.0.1.18" biblename="King James 2000" type="x-bible">
  <BIBLEBOOK bnumber="26">
    <CHAPTER cnumber="2">
      <VERS vnumber="1">And he said unto me, <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Son of man, stand upon your feet, and I will speak unto you.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="2">And the Spirit entered into me when he spoke unto me, and set me upon my feet, that I heard him that spoke unto me.</VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="3">And he said unto me, <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">Son of man, I send you to the children of Israel, to a rebellious nation that has rebelled against me: they and their fathers have transgressed against me, even unto this very day.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="4">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">For they are impudent children and stubborn. I do send you unto them; and you shall say unto them, Thus says the Lord GOD.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="5">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">And they, whether they will hear, or whether they refuse, (for they are a rebellious house,) yet shall know that there has been a prophet among them.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="6">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">And you, son of man, be not afraid of them, neither be afraid of their words, though briers and thorns are with you, and you do dwell among scorpions: be not afraid of their words, nor be dismayed at their looks, though they be a rebellious house.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="7">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">And you shall speak my words unto them, whether they will hear, or whether they refuse: for they are most rebellious.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="8">
        <STYLE css="color:#FF0000">But you, son of man, hear what I say unto you; Be not you rebellious like that rebellious house: open your mouth, and eat what I give you.</STYLE>
      </VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="9">And when I looked, behold, a hand was sent unto me; and, lo, a scroll of a book was in it;</VERS>
      <VERS vnumber="10">And he spread it before me; and it was written inside and outside: and there was written in it lamentations, and mourning, and woe.</VERS>
    </CHAPTER>
  </BIBLEBOOK>
</XMLBIBLE>